<title>USA: Coca-Cola FEMSA files for $175 mln notes.</title>
<headline>Coca-Cola FEMSA files for $175 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coca-Cola FEMSA SA de CV of Mexico said Thursday it filed a registration with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission for up to $175 million in notes due 2006.</p>
<p>The offering will be made through J.P. Morgan &amp; Co, Bear, Stearns &amp; Co Inc and Morgan Stanley &amp; Co Inc, the filing said.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used to repay all of its outstanding indebtedness incurred in the form of a U.S. dollar-demoninated borrowing under a credit facility, the filing said. Any remaining balance will be used for general corporate purposes.</p>
</text>
